{"name":"Baroness","hex":"#a785a7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baroness","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The wife of a baron.","A woman holding a baronial title in her own right; a female ruler of a barony."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baroness"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baroness (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Baroness is an American heavy metal band from Savannah, Georgia that has been active since 2003. Its early members grew up together in Lexington, Virginia. The band has undergone numerous lineup changes, with frontman John Baizley serving as the sole constant throughout. Baizley creates the artwork for all of the group's albums and has done artwork for other bands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/2018_RiP_-_Baroness_-_by_2eight_-_8SC7490.jpg/330px-2018_RiP_-_Baroness_-_by_2eight_-_8SC7490.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baroness_(band)","wikidata":"Q808701"},{"title":"Baroness (G.I. Joe)","blocks":[{"text":"Baroness is a fictional character from the G.I. Joe: A Real American Hero toyline by Hasbro, originally appearing in the first issue of the G.I. Joe: A Real American Hero comic series by Marvel Comics in June, 1982. The Baroness is a villainess, associated with the G.I. Joe Team's nemesis, Cobra."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/45/GIJoeBaronessRAH.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baroness_(G.I._Joe)","wikidata":"Q4353475"},{"title":"Baron","blocks":[{"text":"Baron is a rank of nobility or title of honour, often hereditary, in various European countries, either current or historical. The female equivalent is baroness. Typically, the title denotes an aristocrat who ranks higher than a lord or knight, but lower than a viscount or count. Often, barons hold their fief – their lands and income – directly from the monarch. Barons are less often the vassals of other nobles. In many kingdoms, they were entitled to wear a smaller form of a crown called a coronet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Heraldic_Crown_of_Spanish_Barons.svg/330px-Heraldic_Crown_of_Spanish_Barons.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baron","wikidata":"Q165503"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Baroness_Coachella_2010.jpeg/500px-Baroness_Coachella_2010.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Baroness_Coachella_2010.jpeg/1280px-Baroness_Coachella_2010.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Baroness_Coachella_2010.jpeg/500px-Baroness_Coachella_2010.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baroness at Coachella Festival 2010","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaroness_Coachella_2010.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Baroness_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg/500px-Baroness_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Baroness_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg/1280px-Baroness_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Baroness_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg/500px-Baroness_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"John Baizley at Roadburn Festival 2017","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaroness_%40_Roadburn_Festival_2017_06.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Archive-ugent-be-79D46426-CC9D-11E3-B56B-4FBAD43445F2_DS-0_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Archive-ugent-be-79D46426-CC9D-11E3-B56B-4FBAD43445F2_DS-0_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Archive-ugent-be-79D46426-CC9D-11E3-B56B-4FBAD43445F2_DS-0_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Archive-ugent-be-79D46426-CC9D-11E3-B56B-4FBAD43445F2_DS-0_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lord of Parliament, also called a baron, illustrated in the manuscript \"Théâtre de tous les peuples et nations de la terre avec leurs habits et ornemens divers, tant anciens que modernes, diligemment depeints au naturel\". Painted by Lucas d'Heere in the second half of the 16th century. Preserved in the Ghent University Library.[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArchive-ugent-be-79D46426-CC9D-11E3-B56B-4FBAD43445F2_DS-0_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Wenceslas_Hollar_-_A_baron_%28State_1%29.jpg/500px-Wenceslas_Hollar_-_A_baron_%28State_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Wenceslas_Hollar_-_A_baron_%28State_1%29.jpg/1280px-Wenceslas_Hollar_-_A_baron_%28State_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Wenceslas_Hollar_-_A_baron_%28State_1%29.jpg/500px-Wenceslas_Hollar_-_A_baron_%28State_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The robe worn by a baron during his creation ceremony in 17th-century Britain, engraved by Wenceslas Hollar.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWenceslas_Hollar_-_A_baron_(State_1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https: